Bash	git ls-files && cat billing/*.py accounts/*.py && grep -rn "get_invoice_total\|vat\|sign_up" --include=*.py . ; ls; cat CLAUDE.md AGENTS.md 2>/dev/null; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3
Bash	grep -rn "get_invoice_total\|vat\|sign_up" . --exclude-dir=.git; cat README.md orders/total.py; git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3
text	All three findings match the code. They are outside the `orders` module, so the rules make them issues, not fixes on this branch. I load the github skill to file them.
Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/filing.md
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/tracker.md; ls $D/scripts
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/collect.sh filing billing/tax.py accounts/signup.py vat sign_up cents email 2>&1 | tail -5; gh repo view acme/shop --json visibility --jq .visibility; gh label list
Bash	cat <tmp>/collect.SGSSNf
text	No existing issue covers them. I file two new issues.
Bash	T=$(mktemp -d) && cat > $T/vat.md <<'EOF'; `billing/tax.py:4`: the docstring of `vat` says that it returns the VAT "in cents". The function returns euros, as a `Decimal` quantized to `0.01`. Its only caller, `get_invoice_total` in `billing/invoice.py:5`, adds the result to an order total in euros.; ; A reader who trusts the docstring can divide the result by 100, or multiply a euro amount by 100 before the call. The docstring must say euros.; ; Out of scope for #14: found by the review of the branch for #14, which changes only the `orders` module.; EOF; cat > $T/signup.md <<'EOF'; `accounts/signup.py:4`: `sign_up` stores the email as typed and checks for duplicates with an exact match. So `Bob@shop.test` and `bob@shop.test` sign up as two accounts.; ; To decide: normalize the email before the check and the store (for example `strip()` and lowercase the domain or the whole address), and say how existing accounts that differ only in case are handled.; ; Out of scope for #14: found by the review of the branch for #14, which changes only the `orders` module.; EOF; gh issue create --repo acme/shop --title "billing: docstring of vat says cents, but it returns euros" --label documentation --body-file $T/vat.md; gh issue create --repo acme/shop --title "accounts: sign_up treats emails that differ only in case as two accounts" --label bug --body-file $T/signup.md
text	I checked all three findings against the code and they are all real. All three are outside the `orders` module that #14 changes, so I did not fix them on this branch. Your rules send out-of-scope findings to the tracker. I made no commits and did not touch the branch or the PR.  1. **`get_invoice_total` name**: I filed no issue. It is a nit: only a name, and no project rule asks for the change. If you want an issue for it, file one. 2. **`vat` docstring says cents**: I filed [#17](https://github.com/acme/shop/issues/17) with the `documentation` label. The function returns euros, and its only caller adds the result to a total in euros. 3. **`sign_up` email case**: I filed [#18](https://github.com/acme/shop/issues/18) with the `bug` label. The issue leaves one choice to you: lowercase the whole address or only the domain, and what to do with existing accounts that differ only in case.  Before filing, I searched the tracker for issues on the same code and found none. The repo is public, but the issues hold only this repo's own paths and code.  I changed no code, so I did not run the tests and no docs needed changes.
